Z||000000||NASAReeves||05-24-2001||10:16 PM||||I have an '88GT that is all stock, except for the radio & speakers.  The guage covers (and radio, and console) are the type that have a black background, and a dot-matrix-type pattern of white dots on them.  They are starting to look worn and unsightly.<P>I'm wanting to replace them.  I don't really like the brushed aluminum look (no offense, guys). I've seen on e-bay in the past advertisments of "carbon fiber."  Does anyone have a picture of a "carbon fiber" pattern?  Can anyone tell me where to buy it if I like it?<P>Thanks!<P>------------------<BR>Scott & Traci<BR>'88 GT||||reg||2
Z||000001||Jay||05-24-2001||10:53 PM||||Company I used is called Folia-Tech.  Looks real and comes in unreal colors too.<P>------------------<BR>Jay<BR>1986 Northstar GT<BR>www.members.home.net/jaygrande||||reg||1
Z||000002||cadaver||05-24-2001||11:10 PM||||The stuff on ebay right now is a vinyl sticker. Does not look like carbon. Looks like square dots.||||reg||1
